untry preparedness and readiness of Nepal for responding to COVID-19 pandemic. Preparedness and readiness of government of Nepal designated COVID hospitals 2020. http://nhrc.gov.np/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/Fact-sheet-Preparedness-and-Readiness-of-Government-of-Nepal-Designated-COVID-Hospitals.pdf Available at: Accessed October 25, 2020. 18. The World Bank. Physicians (per 1,000 people) - Nepal. https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/SH.MED.PHYS.ZS?locations=NP Available at: Accessed October 19, 2020. 19. Remuzzi A., Remuzzi G. COVID-19 and Italy: what next? Lancet. 2020;395:1225–1228. doi: 10.1016/S0140-6736(20)30627-9. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Sahu A.K., Amrithanand V.T., Mathew R., et al. COVID-19 in health care workers: a systematic review and meta-analysis. Am J Emerg Med. 2020;38:1727–1731. doi: 10.1016/j.ajem.2020.05.113. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Usuzaki T., Chiba S., Shimoyama M., et al. A disparity in the number of studies related to COVID-19 and SARS-CoV-2 between low- and middle-income countries and high-income countries. Int Health. 2020 doi: 10.1093/inthealth/ihaa088. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Gomersall C.D., Tai D.Y., Loo S., et al. Expanding ICU facilities in an epidemic: recommendations based on experience from the SARS epidemic in Hong Kong and Singapore. Intensive Care Med. 2006;32:1004–1013. doi: 10.1007/s00134-006-0134-5. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Hamal P.K., Chaurasia R.B., Pokhrel N., et al. An affordable videolaryngoscope for use during the COVID-19 pandemic. Lancet Glob Health. 2020;8:e893–e894. doi: 10.1016/S2214-109X(20)30259-X. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Saoraya J., Musikatavorn K., Sereeyotin J. Low-cost videolaryngoscope in response to COVID-19 pandemic. West J Emerg Med. 2020;21:817–818. doi: 10.5811/westjem.2020.5.47831. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Schol