, and other tasks), were the most important predictors of dementia, followed by functioning (competence in daily activities), sociodemographics (education), and APOE status. APOEε2 carrier status predicted dementia development before death, while the ε3ε3 genotype was protective against dementia development, although AUCs were relatively low. The impact of APOEε2 and other major predictors was similar in further analyses considering clinical diagnosis of AD and vascular dementia separately (results not shown). Table 2. Dementia prediction model Predictors AUC [95% CI] Sensitivity [95% CI] Specificity [95% CI] Entire model a 0.73 [0.68–0.78] 0.66 [0.63–0.69] 0.68 [0.66–0.71] Cognition b 0.72 [0.66–0.78] 0.55 [0.51–0.59] 0.55 [0.52–0.58] MMSE Calculation c 0.60 [0.53–0.68] 0.53 [0.49–0.56] 0.68 [0.66–0.70] MMSE Orientation c 0.64 [0.58–0.70] 0.68 [0.65–0.71] 0.54 [0.51–0.56] MMSE Other tasks c 0.65 [0.58–0.72] 0.56 [0.53–0.58] 0.67 [0.65–0.69] MMSE Wordlist c 0.68 [0.62–0.75] 0.77 [0.75–0.80] 0.57 [0.55–0.60] SPMSQ c 0.71 [0.65–0.77] 0.67 [0.65–0.70] 0.64 [0.62–0.67] MMSE total c 0.71 [0.64–0.77] 0.62 [0.59–0.65] 0.61 [0.58–0.63] Functioning b 0.61 [0.55–0.67] 0.62 [0.59–0.65] 0.61 [0.58–0.63] Competence in daily activities c 0.61 [0.55–0.67] 0.83 [0.81–0.86] 0.35 [0.32–0.38] Sociodemographics b 0.60 [0.54–0.65] 0.83 [0.81–0.86] 0.35 [0.32–0.38] Education, years c 0.60 [0.54–0.65] 0.66 [0.63–0.69] 0.68 [0.66–0.71] APOE genotype b 0.58 [0.52–0.64] 0.45 [0.42–0.47] 0.69 [0.67–0.71] APOEε2 carriers c 0.56 [0.51–0.61] 0.25 [0.23–0.27] 0.88 [0.86–0.89] APOEε3ε3 genotype c 0.57 [0.51–0.63] 0.45 [0.42–0.47] 0.69 [0.67–0.71] All genotypes c,d ( 23 / 24 / 33 / 34 / 44 ) 0.58 [0.51–0.64] 0.67 [0.64–0.70] 0.66 [0.63–0.68] Open in a new tab Abbreviations : APOE Apoliprotein E, MMSE Mini Mental State Examination, SPMSQ Short Portable Mental Status Questionnaire AUC, sensitivity and specificity [95% CI] values using the cutoff point Disease State Index (DSI) = 0.5 are shown for 10 